---
const reviewedDate = '2026-07-11';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'How much paint do I need for a 12x12 room?',
    answer: 'A 12x12 room with 8-foot ceilings has 384 square feet of wall area before openings are removed. With one door, two average windows, two coats, and a small reserve, two gallons is a sensible starting estimate. Check the coverage range on your paint before buying.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What coverage rate should I use?',
    answer: 'Many interior paints list a range near 350 to 400 square feet per gallon on a smooth, prepared surface. Porous drywall, masonry, heavy texture, strong color changes, and application technique can lower that figure. The product label or technical data sheet should take priority over the calculator default.',
  },
  {
    question: 'When should I use primer?',
    answer: 'Primer is useful on new drywall, stained or patched surfaces, glossy finishes, bare wood, and major color changes. A paint-and-primer label does not replace a dedicated primer in every situation, so check the product instructions.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How many coats should I plan for?',
    answer: 'Two coats is a sensible plan for most interior walls. A similar color may cover in one coat, while bare drywall, strong color changes, and repaired surfaces can need primer or another coat. Test a small area before buying less paint.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does more expensive paint cover more area?',
    answer: 'Not necessarily. Higher-priced paints may offer better washability, leveling, or hide, but coverage varies by product, color, surface, and application. Use the coverage range printed on the can or technical data sheet.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How does wall texture affect the estimate?',
    answer: 'Texture increases surface area and leaves more low spots for paint to fill. The calculator reduces its assumed coverage as texture gets heavier. Treat that adjustment as a buffer, then compare it with the paint manufacturer\'s guidance for your surface.',
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((faq) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: faq.question,
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: faq.answer,
    },
  })),
  datePublished: '2025-12-26',
  dateModified: reviewedDate,
};
---

<section id="faq" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 md:py-16">
  <div class="text-center mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-heading mb-3">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <p class="text-body max-w-2xl mx-auto">Notes on the assumptions behind the calculator and where your project may differ.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-4">
    {faqs.map((faq) => (
      <details class="group bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-border overflow-hidden">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-5 cursor-pointer hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors">
          <h3 class="text-left font-semibold text-heading pr-4">{faq.question}</h3>
          <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-primary/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 pt-2 border-t border-border">
          <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">{faq.answer}</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p class="text-center text-xs text-gray-400 mt-8">Last checked: July 11, 2026 by Zack Pearson</p>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
</section>
